    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Priya's Music Webpage\r\n\r\nPriya wants to make a webpage about her favorite music but doesn't know how to write HTML or CSS. Instead, they've provided you with a description and a potential screenshot:\r\n\r\n> \"I want to make a webpage about my favorite music because I love sharing what I'm listening to with other people. I want each genre to have its own title with the artists listed underneath. The titles should look different from the artist names — maybe a fancier font. And the artist names should be a warm color, like gold or orange.\"\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/85d3712fe1f9011a73ed96f020d83db6-image-1774473713632.png\" style=\"width: 30%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1) Use AI tutor to help build this page. Ask it to make changes to this page step-by-step.\r\n    - Be specific about the elements, sizes, borders, and which elements they apply to\r\n2) Keep prompting until the webpage it's \"close enough\" to their vision!\r\n    - It doesn't have to perfectly match the image, but try to get it close to the style and layout!\r\n\r\nOnce you've compared your result to Priya's vision: press the Continue button!\r\n\r\n**Hint:** This puzzle involves `<ul>` and `<h2>` tags in HTML, and the `font-family` and `color` properties in CSS.\r\n",
